<p>First of all apologies for necroposting.</p>
<p>Just wanted to add that we don't even know for sure if there even was a big bang nor do we know the head death would be the actual end of the universe, we are merely hypothesizing all that based on the cosmic background radiation, the current expansion of the universe and the increase of entropy.</p>
<p>But what if the Big Bounce is the correct answer?</p>
<p>Conservation of Entropy might very well be true and Carnot Convection is actually happening, it's just taking a rrreeeaaallllllyyy lllooonnnggg time.</p>
<p>Pre Event 4039-1 still violates the second law of thermodynamics tho, I demand an abstract of Dr. Remi's lecture.</p>

